---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy & Disclaimer" description={`How ${site.name} handles your information, and the nature of the numerology readings offered on this site.`}>
  <section class="page-hero night stars">
    <div class="container narrow stack" style="--stack: var(--space-4)">
      <p class="eyebrow">The small print, kept simple</p>
      <h1>Privacy &amp; <em>disclaimer</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section paper">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <h2>Your reading stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The numerology calculator runs entirely in your web browser. The name and date of birth you enter are used only to
        calculate your numbers on your own device; they are <strong>never sent to a server</strong>, and no account is needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        So that you can revisit your reading while you browse, your details are kept in your browser’s
        <em>session storage</em> for the current tab only. They are erased automatically when you close the tab or
        window, and you can erase them at any time with “Forget my details now” at the bottom of your reading.
        No cookies are used for this.
      </p>
      <p>PDF reports are also created in your browser and saved directly to your device.</p>

      <h2>Enquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you send an enquiry through the contact page, the details you choose to share (such as your name, email address
        and message) are used only to reply to you. Depending on how the site is configured, the form either opens your own
        email app or passes your message to a form-delivery service so that it can reach {site.name}.
      </p>

      <h2>About the readings</h2>
      <p>
        Numerology is a traditional, symbolic practice. The readings on this site are based on the Pythagorean method and
        on meanings traditionally associated with each number. They are offered for <strong>entertainment, inspiration and
        self-reflection</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Readings describe themes and tendencies, not certainties.</li>
        <li>They do not predict specific events, and are not scientifically established.</li>
        <li>They are not a substitute for professional medical, legal, financial or psychological advice.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Please use your own judgement, and take only what feels meaningful to you.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about this page, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-hero { position: relative; padding-block: var(--space-8); }
</style>
